          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 26:18",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Uzziah was wroth, and had a censer in his hand to burn incense: and while he was wroth with the priests, the leprosy even rose up in his forehead before the priests in the house of the Lord, from beside the incense altar.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 30
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 26:19",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And Azariah the chief priest, and all the priests, looked upon him, and, behold, he was leprous in his forehead, and they thrust him out from thence; yea, himself hasted also to go out, because the Lord had smitten him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 207,
            "end": 214,
            "text": "TG Punish."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 87
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Punish.",
            "prettyString": "TG Punish",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Punish",
                "entryId": "tg-punish",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 26:20",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And Uzziah the king was a leper unto the day of his death, and dwelt in a several house, being a leper; for he was cut off from the house of the Lord: and Jotham his son was over the king’s house, judging the people of the land.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "TG Leprosy."
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "HEB separate."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 94
          },
          {
            "start": 170,
            "end": 173
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Leprosy.",
            "prettyString": "TG Leprosy",
            "references": [
